        "evidence_contexts": [
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_introduction_index_b025",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_introduction",
            "content_sha256": "c1954773f59b7946b486a645bf57b22c8c8c8a8282feaa25b4b5ef36afd61934",
            "context_id": "ctx_305c430849e3734c0aa7afaf",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "POSITIVE_DEFINITION_PROPOSAL",
              "POSITIVE_POS_PROPOSAL",
              "PRIMARY"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "dimensionality",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_5700a426581db0e5405886b2",
            "source_text": "When every example is characterized by the same number of numerical values,\nwe say that the data consist of fixed-length vectors\nand we describe the constant length of the vectors\nas the *dimensionality* of the data.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_convolutional_neural_networks_why_conv_b024",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_convolutional_neural_networks",
            "content_sha256": "f88647e9668714d70941323834cfba6ed0fd9c1220d3470b893298317eebd7af",
            "context_id": "ctx_3923942a6da07182f6169b13",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "BACKUP"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "dimensionality",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_9f5becd63a4c7ebe588de85a",
            "source_text": "While previously, we might have required billions of parameters\nto represent just a single layer in an image-processing network,\nwe now typically need just a few hundred, without\naltering the dimensionality of either\nthe inputs or the hidden representations.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_deep_learning_computation_deferred_init_b003",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_deep_learning_computation",
            "content_sha256": "14b037c0cf46c0e97af1f01bcade0e074bdf5868f3e05c73429fa27a5d6e8a9e",
            "context_id": "ctx_4d511a9e270716621c12b480",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "PRIMARY"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "dimensionality",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_669fc705ed1d247da76a2a0f",
            "source_text": "* We defined the network architectures\n  without specifying the input dimensionality.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_linear_networks_linear_regression_b090",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_linear_networks",
            "content_sha256": "a9b4023298af39c7259bd8914b8cc3a3283df5d11e279c0ae04ce4ca2ce6c47a",
            "context_id": "ctx_571461d7592e0eb07fae9808",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "POSITIVE_DEFINITION_PROPOSAL",
              "PRIMARY"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "dimensionality",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_e2345e6aa1792a8c68b3a919",
            "source_text": "For the neural network shown in :numref:`fig_single_neuron`,\nthe inputs are $x_1, \\ldots, x_d$,\nso the *number of inputs* (or *feature dimensionality*) in the input layer is $d$.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_preliminaries_linear_algebra_b022",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_preliminaries",
            "content_sha256": "f9eaf45fa0c3085530f83756eea266b91333ed63a740862b6e2e661f92327673",
            "context_id": "ctx_9a25a4253bc511ca8268d02a",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "POSITIVE_POS_PROPOSAL",
              "PRIMARY"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "dimensionality",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_c0c69e53d0a3344cac8170d5",
            "source_text": "### Length, Dimensionality, and Shape",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_convolutional_modern_googlenet_b012",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_convolutional_modern",
            "content_sha256": "af2ae9b06b4b5a9f61507fd4ae59664cbff415fd53b25ca5ba424a3715708936",
            "context_id": "ctx_bc1664e975977f0d9d0df8c9",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "BACKUP"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "dimensionality",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_7746e3daea3383a70cdda573",
            "source_text": "Maximum pooling between inception blocks reduces the dimensionality.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_multilayer_perceptrons_weight_decay_b025",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_multilayer_perceptrons",
            "content_sha256": "f1a24477304c26ef1820b379c136348db6d3dcd698be96fb358e52250fe47a84",
            "context_id": "ctx_cf2fee46db0f41e6ec64a579",
            "evidence_roles": [
              "PRIMARY"
            ],
            "matched_surface": "dimensionality",
            "positive_evidence_eligible": true,
            "sentence_id": "sentence_8106df143bde2e828a585a2a",
            "source_text": "To make the effects of overfitting pronounced,\nwe can increase the dimensionality of our problem to $d = 200$\nand work with a small training set containing only 20 examples.",
            "synthetic": false
          },
          {
            "block_id": "d2l_recurrent_neural_networks_rnn_scratch_b036",
            "boundary_only": false,
            "chapter_id": "d2l_recurrent_neural_networks",
